// Azure Resource Graph Query
// VM v6/v7 Modernization Readiness — Discover, Assess, and full inventory signals
//
// WHAT IT DOES
//   Returns one row per Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines resource (standalone
//   VMs, Availability Set members, and VMSS Flex members) and one row per
//   Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachineScaleSets/virtualMachines resource (VMSS
//   Uniform-mode members), each with:
//     1. The signals the plugin uses to compute its derived readiness columns
//        (workload pattern, Hyper-V generation, disk controller type, series
//        generation, Azure Disk Encryption, execution-method recommendation,
//        target SKU, lifecycle/pricing notes)
//     2. The full raw inventory signal set from the Assess article's own
//        "Inventory query (Azure Resource Graph)" starter query (placement,
//        OS/image, storage, capabilities/licensing, networking, security),
//        surfaced as-is so a reader has everything that article's checklist
//        references, not only the subset the plugin's own verdicts consume.
//     3. For every VMSS-backed row (Flex or Uniform), the parent scale set's
//        orchestration mode and model/default VM profile size, joined in via
//        the row's own derived scale-set ID (see the VMSS-parent join below).
//
// NOTES
//   - Hyper-V generation and disk controller type are confirmed directly
//     queryable via properties.extended.instanceView.hyperVGeneration and
//     properties.storageProfile.diskControllerType (live-tenant spike, see
//     research evidence C11) — no supplementary Compute API call is needed.
//     This was confirmed against Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines rows;
//     whether Uniform-mode instance rows populate the same instanceView
//     fields identically has not been separately live-tenant-verified (open
//     risk, tracked in the plan's Risks and Open Questions).
//   - Two independent Azure Disk Encryption (ADE) signals are surfaced:
//       * AzureDiskEncryption: aggregated across every attached disk (OS +
//         data), read from the managed disk resource's
//         properties.encryptionSettingsCollection.enabled, joined to the VM
//         by managedBy (same join pattern as the existing APRL query
//         f0a97179-133a-6e4f-8a49-8a44da73ffce.kql) and summarized with max()
//         before the join to avoid duplicating VM rows. This is NOT the same
//         as the VM-resident encryptionAtHost property.
//       * ADEOSDiskEnabled: the OS-disk-only signal the Assess article's own
//         starter query reads directly off the VM via
//         properties.storageProfile.osDisk.encryptionSettings.enabled — no
//         join needed, but it misses data-disk-only encryption.
//     Both are kept so a reader can cross-check the simpler (OS-disk-only)
//   - OSDiskType/OSDiskSizeGB are joined from the managed disk resource
//     (filtered to OS disks via properties.osType, which only OS disks
//     carry), not read off the VM's embedded storageProfile as the Assess
//     article's starter query does. A live-tenant spike showed the VM's own
//     storageProfile.osDisk.managedDisk.storageAccountType/diskSizeGB are
//     frequently absent from the ARM response even though the disk resource
//     itself reports both reliably — this join is a deliberate accuracy
//     improvement over the article's verbatim query. The VM-embedded values
//     remain as a fallback (iff/coalesce) for the rare case the disk
//     resource can't be joined.
//     signal against the more complete (any-disk) one.
//   - Uniform-orchestration VMSS member instances
//     (microsoft.compute/virtualmachinescalesets/virtualmachines) are NOT
//     queryable from the `resources` table — Azure Resource Graph's own
//     table reference places this exact type in the separate
//     `computeresources` table (confirmed against Microsoft's published ARG
//     table/type reference), the same kind of table split
//     `kql/discover-assess-avd.kql`'s AVD host-pool lookup already handles
//     (`desktopvirtualizationresources` instead of `resources`). The two
//     sources are combined with a top-level
//     `union` so every row still reaches the one shared derived-column and
//     classification path with `HasScaleSet` forced to true for Uniform rows.
//     A Uniform instance has no properties.virtualMachineScaleSet.id of its
//     own (that property is Flex-only); its parent scale-set ID is instead
//     derived by trimming the instance's own resource ID at
//     "/virtualmachines/" (the ID embeds
//     .../virtualMachineScaleSets/<name>/virtualMachines/<instanceId>), the
//     same string-derivation technique `kql/discover-assess-avd.kql`'s AVD
//     host-pool lookup already uses for a child-to-parent ID relationship.
(
resources
| where type =~ "microsoft.compute/virtualmachines"
)
| union (
computeresources
| where type =~ "microsoft.compute/virtualmachinescalesets/virtualmachines"
)
| extend vmId = tolower(id)
| extend p = properties
| extend isUniformMember = type =~ "microsoft.compute/virtualmachinescalesets/virtualmachines"
// ---- v1 derived-column signals (pattern classification, series, ADE-any-disk) ----
| extend isAKSManaged = isnotnull(tags["aks-managed-poolName"]) or isnotnull(tags["aks-managed-cluster-name"])
| extend isDatabricksManaged = tags["Vendor"] =~ "Databricks"
| extend hasScaleSet = isnotnull(p.virtualMachineScaleSet.id) or isUniformMember
// ---- identity & placement (Assess starter query) ----
| extend
    availabilityZone    = tostring(zones[0]),
    availabilitySetId   = tostring(p.availabilitySet.id),
    // Lowercased (matching the NIC join's tolower(properties.virtualMachine.id)
    // convention below) because this is an ARM-embedded property value, not
    // the resources table's own normalized `id` column the VMSS-parent join's
    // right side keys on via tolower(id) — case-sensitive Kusto join keys
    // would otherwise silently fail to match for VMSS Flex rows.
    vmssIdFlex          = tolower(tostring(p.virtualMachineScaleSet.id)),
    platformFaultDomain = tostring(p.platformFaultDomain)
// Uniform rows carry no vmssIdFlex property; derive the parent scale set's ID
// by trimming this instance's own ID at "/virtualmachines/" instead.
| extend
    vmssId = case(
        isnotempty(vmssIdFlex), vmssIdFlex,
        isUniformMember,        substring(vmId, 0, indexof(vmId, "/virtualmachines/")),
                                 '')
| extend
    availabilitySetName = iff(isnotempty(availabilitySetId), tostring(split(availabilitySetId, '/')[-1]), ''),
    vmssName            = iff(isnotempty(vmssId),            tostring(split(vmssId, '/')[-1]), '')
| extend
    membershipModel = case(
        isUniformMember,                'VMSS (Uniform)',
        isnotempty(vmssId),             'VMSS Flex',
        isnotempty(availabilitySetId),  'Availability Set',
                                         'Standalone'),
    zonePlacement   = iff(isnotempty(availabilityZone), 'Zonal', 'Regional')
// ---- compute & generation ----
| extend
    vmSize           = tostring(p.hardwareProfile.vmSize),
    hyperVGeneration = tostring(p.extended.instanceView.hyperVGeneration)
// ---- power state + data quality ----
| extend vmState = tostring(p.extended.instanceView.powerState.displayStatus)
| extend instanceViewCaptured = iff(isempty(hyperVGeneration) and isempty(vmState), 'No', 'Yes')
// ---- OS & image ----
| extend
    osType          = tostring(p.storageProfile.osDisk.osType),
    osVersion       = tostring(p.extended.instanceView.osVersion),
    computerName    = tostring(p.extended.instanceView.computerName),
    isMarketplaceVm = isnotempty(plan),
    imagePublisher  = tostring(p.storageProfile.imageReference.publisher),
    imageOffer      = tostring(p.storageProfile.imageReference.offer),
    imageSku        = tostring(p.storageProfile.imageReference.sku),
    imageVersion    = tostring(p.storageProfile.imageReference.exactVersion)
// ---- storage / disks ----
// NOTE: osDiskType/osDiskSizeGB below are read from the VM's own embedded
// storageProfile, matching the Assess article's starter query verbatim. A
// live-tenant spike confirmed these VM-embedded fields are frequently absent
// from the ARM response even when the OS disk itself has a SKU/size — the
// Microsoft.Compute/disks resource is the authoritative source. The OS-disk
// join below (filtered on properties.osType, which only OS disks carry)
// supplies the authoritative value, and these VM-embedded fields remain only
// as a fallback for the rare case the disk resource itself can't be joined.
| extend
    diskControllerType = tostring(p.storageProfile.diskControllerType),
    osDiskTypeVMProperty   = tostring(p.storageProfile.osDisk.managedDisk.storageAccountType),
    osDiskSizeGBVMProperty = toint(p.storageProfile.osDisk.diskSizeGB),
    ephemeralOsDisk     = iff(tostring(p.storageProfile.osDisk.diffDiskSettings.option) =~ 'Local', 'Yes', 'No'),
    dataDiskCount       = array_length(p.storageProfile.dataDisks),
    adeOsDiskEnabled    = tostring(p.storageProfile.osDisk.encryptionSettings.enabled)
// ---- capabilities / licensing ----
| extend
    hibernationEnabled = tostring(p.additionalCapabilities.hibernationEnabled),
    ultraSsdEnabled    = tostring(p.additionalCapabilities.ultraSSDEnabled),
    licenseType        = tostring(p.licenseType)
// ---- network (VM level) ----
| extend nicCount = array_length(p.networkProfile.networkInterfaces)
// ---- security & encryption ----
| extend
    securityType      = tostring(p.securityProfile.securityType),
    secureBootEnabled = tostring(p.securityProfile.uefiSettings.secureBootEnabled),
    vTpmEnabled       = tostring(p.securityProfile.uefiSettings.vTpmEnabled)
| project
    vmId,
    vmssId,
    Name = name,
    Id = id,
    ResourceGroup = resourceGroup,
    SubscriptionId = subscriptionId,
    Location = location,
    VMSize = vmSize,
    HyperVGeneration = hyperVGeneration,
    DiskControllerType = diskControllerType,
    HasScaleSet = hasScaleSet,
    IsAKSManaged = isAKSManaged,
    IsDatabricksManaged = isDatabricksManaged,
    MembershipModel = membershipModel,
    ZonePlacement = zonePlacement,
    AvailabilityZone = availabilityZone,
    VMSSName = vmssName,
    AvailabilitySetName = availabilitySetName,
    PlatformFaultDomain = platformFaultDomain,
    VMPowerState = vmState,
    InstanceViewCaptured = instanceViewCaptured,
    OSType = osType,
    OSVersion = osVersion,
    ComputerName = computerName,
    IsMarketplaceVM = isMarketplaceVm,
    ImagePublisher = imagePublisher,
    ImageOffer = imageOffer,
    ImageSKU = imageSku,
    ImageVersion = imageVersion,
    OSDiskType = osDiskTypeVMProperty,
    OSDiskSizeGB = osDiskSizeGBVMProperty,
    EphemeralOSDisk = ephemeralOsDisk,
    DataDiskCount = dataDiskCount,
    ADEOSDiskEnabled = adeOsDiskEnabled,
    HibernationEnabled = hibernationEnabled,
    UltraSSDEnabled = ultraSsdEnabled,
    LicenseType = licenseType,
    NICCount = nicCount,
    SecurityType = securityType,
    SecureBootEnabled = secureBootEnabled,
    VTpmEnabled = vTpmEnabled
// ---- disk join: ADE aggregated across every attached disk (OS + data) ----
| join kind=leftouter (
    resources
    | where type =~ "microsoft.compute/disks"
    | project vmId = tolower(managedBy), diskEncrypted = iff(properties.encryptionSettingsCollection.enabled == true, true, false)
    | summarize AzureDiskEncryption = max(diskEncrypted) by vmId
  ) on vmId
// ---- OS disk join: authoritative SKU/size from the managed disk resource
// itself (properties.osType is present only on OS disks, never data disks,
// so this reliably isolates the one OS disk per VM) ----
| join kind=leftouter (
    resources
    | where type =~ "microsoft.compute/disks"
    | where isnotempty(properties.osType)
    | project vmId = tolower(managedBy), osDiskTypeDisk = tostring(sku.name), osDiskSizeGBDisk = toint(properties.diskSizeGB)
  ) on vmId
// ---- NIC join: any attached NIC with accelerated networking / IP forwarding ----
| join kind=leftouter (
    resources
    | where type =~ "microsoft.network/networkinterfaces"
    | extend nicVmId = tolower(tostring(properties.virtualMachine.id))
    | where isnotempty(nicVmId)
    | summarize
        anyAccelNet = countif(tobool(properties.enableAcceleratedNetworking) == true),
        anyIpFwd    = countif(tobool(properties.enableIPForwarding) == true)
      by vmId = nicVmId
  ) on vmId
// NOTE: the AVD host-pool-type signal (Microsoft.DesktopVirtualization/hostPools
// and .../hostPools/sessionHosts) is intentionally NOT joined here. Those types
// live in the desktopvirtualizationresources table, and Azure Resource Graph
// disallows referencing more than one non-"resources" extension table in the
// same query (confirmed live: querying computeresources together with
// desktopvirtualizationresources in one request fails with
// "UnsupportedRemoteTableScenario ... are unsupported, or disallowed in the
// same cross table queries") — this query already uses computeresources
// above for Uniform-mode VMSS members, so AVD host-pool data is fetched by a
// separate query (discover-assess-avd.kql) and merged onto these rows in Go
// by vmId after both queries return.
// ---- VMSS-parent join: scale-set-level ("pool-level") data joined onto every
// VMSS-backed row (Flex or Uniform) via the row's own derived vmssId, rather
// than a second top-level query/sheet. Rows with no vmssId (standalone VMs,
// Availability Set members) naturally get null join results here, projected
// as "N/A (not pool-managed)" downstream in Go.
// LIMITATION (accepted, not solved by a second query/sheet): a scale set
// with zero current member instances produces no row in this query at all,
// so this join cannot surface that scale set's orchestration mode/model size
// independent of at least one visible member instance.
| join kind=leftouter (
    resources
    | where type =~ "microsoft.compute/virtualmachinescalesets"
    | project vmssId = tolower(id), poolOrchestrationMode = tostring(properties.orchestrationMode), poolModelVMSize = tostring(sku.name)
  ) on vmssId
| project
    Name,
    Id,
    ResourceGroup,
    SubscriptionId,
    Location,
    VMSize,
    HyperVGeneration,
    DiskControllerType,
    HasScaleSet,
    IsAKSManaged,
    IsDatabricksManaged,
    AzureDiskEncryption = iff(isnull(AzureDiskEncryption), false, AzureDiskEncryption),
    MembershipModel,
    ZonePlacement,
    AvailabilityZone,
    VMSSName,
    AvailabilitySetName,
    PlatformFaultDomain,
    VMPowerState,
    InstanceViewCaptured,
    OSType,
    OSVersion,
    ComputerName,
    IsMarketplaceVM,
    ImagePublisher,
    ImageOffer,
    ImageSKU,
    ImageVersion,
    OSDiskType = iff(isnotempty(osDiskTypeDisk), osDiskTypeDisk, OSDiskType),
    OSDiskSizeGB = coalesce(osDiskSizeGBDisk, OSDiskSizeGB),
    EphemeralOSDisk,
    DataDiskCount,
    ADEOSDiskEnabled,
    HibernationEnabled,
    UltraSSDEnabled,
    LicenseType,
    NICCount,
    AcceleratedNetworking = iff(coalesce(anyAccelNet, 0) > 0, 'Yes', 'No'),
    IPForwarding = iff(coalesce(anyIpFwd, 0) > 0, 'Yes', 'No'),
    SecurityType,
    SecureBootEnabled,
    VTpmEnabled,
    OrchestrationMode = poolOrchestrationMode,
    PoolModelVMSize = poolModelVMSize
